#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34f4b65e-b93a-51e8-b943-b3b53d47fffb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "7c937587-dc81-5ee9-aa66-a509a87433e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4067" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $2^{x+1}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_2$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x+1} & =3 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡({2}^{x+1}) & ={log}_{2}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b \\left( b^c \\right) = c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx+1 = \\log_2 \\left( 3 \\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & ={log}_{2}⁡(3) \\\\ x & ={log}_{2}⁡(3)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x= \\log_2 \\left( 3 \\right) - 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110495 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110594 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a7784d8-f6a4-5e45-b03e-d76a27372c48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "45d74b50-fd9d-5d18-835d-a7e140278a34" :question/math-academy-id "e-4069" :question/problem "Given that $3^{2x+3}=5,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_3$ of both sides of the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n   \t3^{2x+3} \t\t\t\t&= 5 \\[3pt]\n\t\\log_3 \\left(3^{2x+3}\\right)\t&= \\log_3 (5) \\[3pt]\n\t2x+3 \t\t\t\t\t&= \\log_3 (5) . \\[3pt]\n}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}-3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx \\approx -0.768\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n**Note:** We used the change of base formula to rewrite the right-hand side, as many calculators can only compute base $10$ logarithms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110496 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110595 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d076e5d-9d08-5355-b813-d1749feb0803" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "5d31a3e8-aae6-50b5-9ce1-65cef1d8395e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4071" :question/problem "Given that $3\\cdot 6^{x} = 9,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {6}^{x} & =9 \\\\ {6}^{x} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n   \t6^x \t\t\t\t\t&= 3 \\[3pt]\n\t\\log_6 \\left(6^x\\right)\t&= \\log_6 (3) \\[3pt]\n\tx \t\t\t\t\t&= \\log_6 (3)\\[3pt]\n}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\log(3)}{\\log(6)}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx \\approx 0.613\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34f4b65e-b93a-51e8-b943-b3b53d47fffb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064a3c82-ae53-5db3-ad5c-b3fcfc6fb6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{5}⁡(4)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544101} {:answer/id #uuid "49f84153-b03e-5266-a48d-c82f2db5b6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544247} {:answer/id #uuid "7b506411-a799-5138-a14f-4b0c6672b0c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544360} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3750bd-081d-5764-9284-5e0451f625eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544522} {:answer/id #uuid "ee944174-45cf-5629-b838-1acad19f5360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(7)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49f84153-b03e-5266-a48d-c82f2db5b6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544247} :answer-field/id #uuid "3300a13e-fe37-59f5-9d51-81da8e4c45f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07d6770c-e373-5366-b946-966ce2aa6000" :question/math-academy-id "q-100163" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation ${7}^{x+4}=5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take ${log}_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{x+4} & =5 \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡({7}^{x+4}) & ={log}_{7}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+4={log}_{7}⁡(5)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & ={log}_{7}⁡(5) \\\\ x & ={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110595 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d076e5d-9d08-5355-b813-d1749feb0803" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "249cec14-666a-5fae-9615-1544a0eec215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544166} {:answer/id #uuid "3755bb99-c614-5cf1-80fc-6be88288dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544208} {:answer/id #uuid "767e7c4e-ad51-5769-a990-6385b5908531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544349} {:answer/id #uuid "b73616bd-6754-5514-aa8a-eead41959119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.740" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544475} {:answer/id #uuid "f6221a2d-763a-5c87-bb34-2b68cf8fa1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.740" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3755bb99-c614-5cf1-80fc-6be88288dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544208} :answer-field/id #uuid "51e41568-3547-5b0e-b361-b42d6abf90f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e1ee8c2-d8a9-5564-8fe2-55ce248be31a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31891" :question/problem "Given that ${5}^{2a+3}-13=25,$ find the value of $a$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2a+3}-13 & =25 \\\\ {5}^{2a+3} & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{5}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2a+3} & =38 \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡({5}^{2a+3}) & ={log}_{5}⁡(38) \\\\ 2a+3 & ={log}_{5}⁡(38)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(38)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)} \\\\ 2a & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(38)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}-3 \\\\ a & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(38)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\na≈-0.370\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34f4b65e-b93a-51e8-b943-b3b53d47fffb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f147060-2e3d-530e-8605-1ba13a4114d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{5}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544364} {:answer/id #uuid "9dec9e09-3ab9-51d5-93f5-5553f7a2ae1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{5}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544429} {:answer/id #uuid "cd163f76-39be-503b-8e02-0fc0fc56c0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{3}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544521} {:answer/id #uuid "d87bd39e-276b-5919-ae48-a488a12d6528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{{log}_{3}⁡(5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544553} {:answer/id #uuid "f4426217-c85d-5fd5-a049-5d1b721018a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd163f76-39be-503b-8e02-0fc0fc56c0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{3}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544521} :answer-field/id #uuid "479444fd-611e-5a03-bcad-55f19ebf647d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4dbd2fd5-279c-5b4f-83af-6acbee35f908" :question/math-academy-id "q-66801" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation ${3}^{x}=5.$" :question/worked-solution "We take ${log}_{3}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & =5 \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡({3}^{x}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx={log}_{3}⁡(5)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110594 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a7784d8-f6a4-5e45-b03e-d76a27372c48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a7be4c-c258-5104-8444-2a5ac6bf1461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.685" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544163} {:answer/id #uuid "78981f9f-c8a0-501c-a93c-1f3d6d8a9843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.604" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544355} {:answer/id #uuid "ca20cb11-444e-5551-a283-109595f4bfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544511} {:answer/id #uuid "d6441217-85f1-5384-af07-4fb4353c7e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544544} {:answer/id #uuid "ddefe1b3-5955-5cb7-9393-02639a571285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.604" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6441217-85f1-5384-af07-4fb4353c7e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544544} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb33b195-f963-5860-8754-612425a1f549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "918c847a-dee1-5e90-aa75-e08ca9d39fd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-66811" :question/problem "Given that ${3}^{4-2x}=\\sqrt{2},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking ${log}_{3}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4-2x} & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡({3}^{4-2x}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 4-2x & ={log}_{3}⁡({2}^{1/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n4-2x=\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\ -2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}-4 \\\\ x & =2-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈1.842\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110595 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d076e5d-9d08-5355-b813-d1749feb0803" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82826981-110c-5a1a-858e-43f3412d0ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{{log}_{4}⁡(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544370} {:answer/id #uuid "9de9a0bc-28a2-5c16-8937-334d75654754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={log}_{4}⁡(33)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544428} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc73e5b-9e38-59e8-b84c-76a4fa387198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={log}_{4}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544562} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f5a6cf-f068-59be-af8a-466cd2c91f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{log}_{4}⁡(11)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544573} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9486c9-bf88-5eab-bce1-b8a6a8aa9b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={log}_{4}⁡(11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea9486c9-bf88-5eab-bce1-b8a6a8aa9b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={log}_{4}⁡(11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544593} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a67648-6807-50b6-a6d7-45ce416912c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f69989d-58f3-5c44-9cd6-bba8083f79ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-66832" :question/problem "Find the exact solution to the equation $3({4}^{y})-14=19.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({4}^{y})-14 & =19 \\\\ 3({4}^{y}) & =33 \\\\ {4}^{y} & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{4}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{y}) & ={log}_{4}⁡(11) \\\\ y & ={log}_{4}⁡(11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y={log}_{4}⁡(11).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110594 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a7784d8-f6a4-5e45-b03e-d76a27372c48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10304769-0b45-5ddb-960a-5561ac8890cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.141" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544119} {:answer/id #uuid "26a853f4-f0a8-5a09-b9c0-56c7fc01358d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.115" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544174} {:answer/id #uuid "66790320-0c2c-5cc3-b140-997d9491efef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.981" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544309} {:answer/id #uuid "945201fd-0d4a-5e7f-a3b1-d14b90583f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.454" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544412} {:answer/id #uuid "feaf6731-e3b7-599f-a042-7ed2790987cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feaf6731-e3b7-599f-a042-7ed2790987cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544643} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4daa940-75d3-59a9-9409-b1cafb9f426c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d436286b-8ea5-5b92-b174-4ebb9b14bf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-973" :question/problem "Given that ${11}^{4-y}=\\sqrt[4]{3},$ find the value of $y$  rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking ${log}_{11}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{11}^{4-y} & =\\sqrt[4]{3} \\\\ {log}_{11}⁡({11}^{4-y}) & ={log}_{11}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{3}) \\\\ 4-y & ={log}_{11}⁡({3}^{1/4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n4-y=\\frac{1}{4}{log}_{11}⁡(3)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} \\\\ -y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}-4 \\\\ y & =4-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈3.885\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}]}
